backend/internal/repository/postgres_evaluation.go: change the EvaluatePreview method signature to add a trailing previewSchema parameter. Pinned exact signature (must match the DBExecutor interface method in validation_service.go, edited in a separate TODO):
`func (r *PostgresRepository) EvaluatePreview(ctx context.Context, studentID int, question models.Question, studentSQL string, sandboxSchema string, previewSchema string) (PreviewResult, error)`
New body (replaces the current 5-line body at ~:225-230):
```go
func (r *PostgresRepository) EvaluatePreview(ctx context.Context, studentID int, question models.Question, studentSQL string, sandboxSchema string, previewSchema string) (PreviewResult, error) {
    if question.Type == "QUERY" {
        schema := previewSchema
        if schema == "" {
            schema = querySchemaFor(question, sandboxSchema)
        }
        return r.evaluateQueryPreview(ctx, question, studentSQL, schema)
    }
    schema := previewSchema
    if schema == "" {
        schema = sandboxSchema
    }
    return r.evaluateDMLPreview(ctx, question, studentSQL, schema)
}
```
Do NOT change evaluateQueryPreview, evaluateDMLPreview, querySchemaFor, Evaluate, evaluateQuery, or evaluateDML in any way — they already accept the target schema as their last argument and this change only affects which schema string EvaluatePreview passes them. Because evaluateDMLPreview calls acquireSchemaEvalLock(ctx, tx, schema) on its schema argument, passing a non-empty previewSchema through automatically keys the shared rebuild-contention lock on the decoy schema A with no additional lock code needed. Back-compat (ARCH-016): when previewSchema=="" this reproduces today's schema resolution byte-for-byte for every non-dual question — that is the load-bearing regression guarantee, verify it is preserved exactly.

backend/internal/controllers/practice_controller.go, four edits:
1. `Preview` (~:135-196): after `schema, ok := ctrl.resolveCategorySchema(c, ctx, question)` succeeds and before building `q := question.AsQuestion()`, compute a single previewSchema string with the resolver written as two EXPLICIT branches (both must appear in code, not collapsed into one expression):
```go
previewSchema := ""
if question.DualSchema && question.CategoryPreviewSchema != "" {
    if hasTables, _ := ctrl.repo.SchemaHasTables(ctx, question.CategoryPreviewSchema); hasTables {
        previewSchema = question.CategoryPreviewSchema
    }
}
if question.DualSchema && previewSchema == "" {
    // Dual-without-decoy fallback (spec 6.1): single-schema fallback to B. The student is
    // never blocked and never told; the lecturer is warned on save instead (see Upsert).
    log.Printf("dual-schema fallback: practice question %d (category %d) has dual_schema=true but no usable decoy; preview running on grading schema B", question.ID, question.CategoryID)
}
```
(add "log" to the import block if not already present). Then change the `ctrl.validator.ValidatePreview(...)` call to pass previewSchema as the new trailing argument: `ctrl.validator.ValidatePreview(ctx, int(student.ID), *q, req.SQLText, schema, previewSchema)`. Submit (~:73-132) is COMPLETELY UNCHANGED — grading always runs on B via the existing ctrl.validator.Validate call, no rows are ever returned from Submit.
2. New handler `ImportCategoryPreviewSchema` (mirror `ImportCategorySchema` ~:558-594 almost exactly): bind the same `{ SQL string \`json:"sql"\` }` request body, read confirmReplace from `c.Query("confirm_replace") == "true"`, call `parityWarning, err := ctrl.repo.ImportSchemaIntoCategoryPreview(c.Request.Context(), id, req.SQL, int(lecturer.ID), confirmReplace)`, map errors with the same switch as ImportCategorySchema (ErrCategoryNotFound->404, ErrSchemaQualifiedName->400, ErrCategoryNotEmpty->409, default->500). On success respond `c.JSON(http.StatusOK, gin.H{"message": "Decoy database imported into category", "parity_warning": parityWarning})` (parityWarning may be an empty string; still include the key). This handler is registered on a route in a separate TODO (cmd/main.go).
3. `LecturerPreview` (~:322-364): add `Schema string \`json:"schema"\`` to the anonymous request struct (empty string means default 'grading', matching today's behavior — do not reject other values, just treat anything other than exactly "preview" as grading). Change the branch that currently does `if req.CategoryID > 0 { rows, err = ctrl.repo.PreviewPracticeCorrectSQL(c.Request.Context(), req.CategoryID, req.Type, req.TargetTable, req.CorrectSQL) }` to pass the new useDecoy argument: `useDecoy := req.Schema == "preview"; if req.CategoryID > 0 { rows, err = ctrl.repo.PreviewPracticeCorrectSQL(c.Request.Context(), req.CategoryID, req.Type, req.TargetTable, req.CorrectSQL, useDecoy) } else { rows, err = ctrl.repo.PreviewCorrectSQL(c.Request.Context(), req.Type, req.TargetTable, req.CorrectSQL) }` (the CategoryID<=0 branch is unaffected by Schema, exactly as today).
4. `Upsert` (~:227-283): after the existing re-read into `saved`, add two computed fields to the JSON response (next to the existing expected_result_status/capture_error keys):
`tw := repository.DMLCorrectSQLTargetTableWarning(saved.Type, saved.CorrectSQL, saved.TargetTable)` added as `"table_warning": tw`, and:
```go
dsw := ""
if saved.DualSchema && saved.CategoryPreviewSchema == "" {
    dsw = "Dual schema is enabled but no decoy schema has been uploaded for this category/exam - previews will use the grading schema until you upload one."
}
```
added as `"dual_schema_warning": dsw`. Both are additive keys on the existing 200 response; the save/capture outcome and status code are unaffected.

backend/internal/controllers/quiz_controller.go, two edits:
1. `PreviewAnswer` (~:275-367): after the existing enrollment/active checks and before the `preview := func(jobCtx context.Context) error { ... }` closure, compute previewSchema TYPE-AWARELY (this is the asymmetry vs. practice: QUERY reads the curriculum, DML mutates the sandbox, so they resolve to two different preview schemas):
```go
previewSchema := ""
if question.DualSchema {
    pc, _ := ctrl.repo.GetExamPreviewCurriculumSchema(ctx, int(*question.ExamID))
    if pc != "" {
        if question.Type == "QUERY" {
            if hasTables, _ := ctrl.repo.SchemaHasTables(ctx, pc); hasTables {
                previewSchema = pc
            }
        } else {
            if err := ctrl.repo.EnsureExamPreviewSandboxReady(ctx, int(*question.ExamID)); err == nil {
                previewSchema = repository.ExamPreviewSandboxName(int(*question.ExamID))
            }
        }
    }
    if previewSchema == "" {
        // Dual-without-decoy fallback (spec 6.1): single-schema fallback to B. Student is
        // never blocked/told; the lecturer is warned on save instead (see lecturer_controller.go).
        log.Printf("dual-schema fallback: exam question %d (exam %d) has dual_schema=true but no usable decoy; preview running on grading schema B", question.ID, int(*question.ExamID))
    }
}
```
(add "log" to the import block if not already present). Then change the existing preview closure body from `vResult, vRows, vCols, vCount, vTrunc, e = ctrl.valService.ValidatePreview(jobCtx, int(student.ID), question, req.SQLText, repository.ExamSandboxName(int(*question.ExamID)))` to pass previewSchema as the new trailing argument: `ctrl.valService.ValidatePreview(jobCtx, int(student.ID), question, req.SQLText, repository.ExamSandboxName(int(*question.ExamID)), previewSchema)`. The `repository.ExamSandboxName(...)` sandboxSchema argument (grading fallback target) is UNCHANGED — only the new trailing previewSchema argument is added. SubmitAnswer (~:193-273) is COMPLETELY UNCHANGED.
2. `GetExamQuestions` (~:92-148, the student-facing handler in this file — NOT the lecturer_controller.go handler of the same name): change the strip loop (~:139-145) from `if questions[i].Type != "QUERY" { questions[i].ExpectedResult = nil; questions[i].ExpectedColumns = nil }` to `if questions[i].Type != "QUERY" || questions[i].DualSchema { questions[i].ExpectedResult = nil; questions[i].ExpectedColumns = nil }` — i.e. also strip both fields whenever DualSchema is true, regardless of type, so a dual QUERY question never ships its captured (B-schema) expected_result/expected_columns to the student payload. correct_sql stripping (`questions[i].CorrectSQL = ""`) is unchanged. The strip applies purely based on the DualSchema flag, so it still applies even while the question is in dual-without-decoy fallback.
